From 850eb67547078f297a84cb0d5701bd216b8b45d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:56:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: the GPU thread's command stream and draws: register
 writes in one loop, dirty vertex buffers only

- DmaPusher::SinkRun: an incrementing method's words the engine only sinks (register writes)
  are taken in one loop instead of a CallMethod call each with the DMA state reloaded after it;
  the state after the run is what the per-word path leaves.
- BufferCache::UpdateVertexBuffers visits only the vertex buffers whose dirty bit is set.
- RasterizerVulkan::CachedVertexFormat remembers MaxwellToVK::VertexFormat by type and size.
- The buffer cache reads Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorAccurate() once a frame, not per FindBuffer.
- PS4 counters: the GPU thread's draws, command words, and words taken in runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
---
